Cross-connection requirements:
(a) Provide standards for the protection of the public potable water supply;
(b) Protect the public potable water system at the service connection by isolating within the consumer's premises actual or potential pollution or contamination that may result from backflow through cross-connection;
(c) Provide the means whereby the consumer may segregate domestic and industrial uses into separate systems to prevent possible pollution or contamination of a private potable water system;
(d) Provide a continuous program of cross-connection control that will systematically and effectively prevent the contamination of the public potable water systems.
(Ord. No. 027-04, § 1, 12-20-04)

